  "claims": {
    "What was simulated": [
      {
        "text": "A phase-only SLM with N = 64 squares shapes light through a scattering sample seen by M = 64 camera points; GGS learns the sample's transmission matrix (the map) from 512 photos, and a fresh map predicts the camera with correlation 0.874.",
        "sources": [
          "main/summary.json:settings.N",
          "main/summary.json:settings.M",
          "main/summary.json:results.L",
          "main/summary.json:results.prediction_correlation"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "The box is held at its target by a PID and a Kalman filter; in the two-hour scenario the room warms by 3 \u00b0C, the cooler fails for 10 min and the user asks for a new target of 20.5 \u00b0C.",
        "sources": [
          "config.py:room_warm_by_C",
          "config.py:cooler_fail_for_s",
          "config.py:new_target_C"
        ]
      }
    ],
    "Thermostat": [
      {
        "text": "With PID 200/4 (real box today) the box never stays inside \u00b10.03 \u00b0C after a step (it swings); in a hold its temperature std is 0.1518 \u00b0C.",
